* arith_int_big.sno — integer-only ARITH window, sized for the 3-arm harness.
* arith_loop.sno's 1M-iteration window is ~13ms, far under the harness MIN_MS,
* so it is UNGRADEABLE by construction. This is the same program shape with a
* window large enough to grade: 100M iterations of int-int rt_add.
* Deterministic checksum, predicted in advance: N ends at the bound = 100000000.
    &TRIM = 1
    &STLIMIT = 999999999
    T1 = TIME()
    N = 0
LOOP    N = N + 1
    N = LT(N, 100000000) N        :S(LOOP)
    T2 = TIME()
    OUTPUT = "iterations: " N
    OUTPUT = "ms: " (T2 - T1)
END
